# Component Conventions

## File Structure
- Each component has its own directory under `src/components/`
- Main component file is always named `index.tsx`
- Import components using the directory path: `import Header from "@/components/Header"`
- shadcn/ui components are in `src/components/ui/` directory

## Component Naming
- Use PascalCase for component names
- Use descriptive names that match their purpose
- Note: `Degrees` component actually contains `Projects` - consider renaming for clarity

## Component Responsibilities
- **Header**: Fixed navigation with minimal logo, social links, and resume button (animated entrance and hover effects)
- **Profile**: Hero section with developer info, skills badges, and profile photo (staggered animations, floating effects)
- **AboutMe**: About section with skills grid, professional background, and icons (hover animations, scroll-triggered entrance)
- **GitHubStats**: Dynamic GitHub statistics via API integration (loading animations, hover effects on stats cards)
- **RecentActivity**: Recent commits and activity from GitHub API (smooth data loading animations)
- **Projects** (in Degrees folder): Project showcase with modern card design and badges (staggered grid, hover effects, featured badge animations)
- **Footer**: Minimal footer with social links, description, and copyright (icon rotation effects, staggered entrance)

## shadcn/ui Integration
- Use shadcn/ui components as base: `Button`, `Card`, `CardContent`, `Badge`
- Import with proper paths: `import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"`
- Use component variants: `variant="ghost"`, `variant="outline"`, `size="sm"`
- Use `asChild` prop for Next.js Link integration: `<Button asChild><Link>...</Link></Button>`
- Wrap shadcn/ui components with motion for animations: `<motion.div><Button /></motion.div>`

## Image Handling
- Import images from `@/img/` directory
- Use Next.js `Image` component with proper width, height, and alt attributes
- Profile photos use `rounded-full` with border and shadow effects
- Project images use responsive sizing and hover effects

## Interactive Elements
- Use shadcn/ui Button component for all buttons
- Use Next.js `Link` component with `asChild` prop for navigation
- External links should have `target="_blank"` and `rel="noopener noreferrer"`
- Use Lucide React icons: `import { Github, Linkedin } from "lucide-react"`
- Apply consistent hover effects and transitions with Framer Motion
- Use `whileHover` and `whileTap` for interactive feedback
- Add icon rotation effects: `whileHover={{ rotate: 360 }}`
- Implement scale effects: `whileHover={{ scale: 1.05 }}`

## Layout Patterns
- Use semantic HTML: `<section>`, `<header>`, `<footer>`, `<main>`
- Apply container classes: `container mx-auto px-6`
- Use consistent spacing: `py-20` for sections, `space-y-4` for elements
- Implement responsive design with proper breakpoints
- Use motion components for animated sections: `<motion.section>`
- Apply scroll-triggered animations: `whileInView` with `viewport={{ once: true }}`
- Implement staggered animations for lists and grids

## Content Structure
- Portuguese language content (pt-br)
- Professional tone appropriate for portfolio
- Consistent spacing and typography hierarchy using shadcn/ui theme
- Dark theme optimized design with proper contrast